text.section:
The Department shall create and distribute educational materials on perinatal and postpartum depression. Such materials shall include:

Fact sheets on symptoms, causes, and available treatment options;


Contact information for local, state, and national resources, including crisis hotlines, counseling services, and support groups;


Guidance for health care providers on screening, diagnosing, and managing perinatal and postpartum depression; and


Information on the impact of untreated perinatal and postpartum depression on maternal and infant health outcomes.

The Department shall distribute materials prepared pursuant to subsection A to:

Health care providers, including obstetricians, midwives, pediatricians, and primary care physicians;


Hospitals, birthing centers, and clinics;


Community organizations, including faith-based groups and nonprofit organizations; and


Public health offices and other relevant government agencies.
